{
  "text": "2010A08 Classify\ndrugs used in the treatment of depression.\nOutline the interactions between anti-depressant drugs and drugs that are\ncommonly used in the peri-operative period.\nAvoid serotonergic drugs\nAvoid indirect acting noradrenergics\nSSRI e.g. fluoxetine\nY\nSNRI e.g. venlafaxine\nY\nY\nNRI e.g. reboxetine\nY\nTCA e.g. amitryptiline\nY\nY\nMAO inhibitor e.g. moclobemide\nY\nY\nDrug\ninteractions:\nSerotonin syndrome\n·\nCause:\n  serotonin reuptake inhibitor + tramadol/pethidine\n·\nFeatures:\no\nCNS (agitation)\no\nANS\n  (↑HR, ↑BP, sweating)\no\nPNS\n  (hyperreflexia, clonus)\no\nGI upset\n  (nausea)\n·\nTreatment:\n  cyproheptadine\nHypertensive crisis\n·\nCause:\n  noradrenaline reuptake inhibitor + indirect acting sympathomimetic amine\n·\nEspecially\n  ephedrine\n·\nAvoid\n  indirect-acting vasopressors, especially ephedrine\n·\nUse\n  direct-acting vasopressors i.e. phenylephrine, noradrenaline\n·\nTreatment:\n  adrenergic antagonist e.g. labetalol, phentolamine\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
